  "result": "All 7 tests pass (the 4 existing plus the 3 new ones).\n\nChanges, all in `editor/buffer.py`:\n\n- **`_Replace` command** added alongside `_Insert` and `_Delete`. It stores the position, the old text, and the new text. Applying it swaps old for new; inverting swaps new for old. This keeps the existing command-pattern design and makes a replace one undo step by construction, rather than composing an insert and a delete.\n- **`replace(pos, n, s)`** validates the range the same way `delete` does, raising IndexError if out of bounds, then executes a `_Replace`. Like other edits, it clears the redo stack.\n- **`history_len()`** returns the length of the undo stack.\n- **`undo_all()`** loops `undo()` until it returns False. Each undone command lands on the redo stack, so the whole history stays redoable.\n\nNothing under `tests/` was touched.",
